  "critique": {
    "axis": "accessibility",
    "evidence": "Economics passes measured keyboard focus, touch-target, viewport-overflow, and reduced-motion checks at all three viewports. However, WCAG color contrast remains unverified: 41 economics nodes are marked serious/incomplete because the gradient prevents measurement. The global header also clips many navigation links at tablet and mobile widths, despite retaining keyboard reachability.",
    "fix": "Replace or simplify gradient-backed surfaces so automated and manual contrast can verify WCAG AA, then remediate every failure. Redesign the tablet/mobile header as an explicitly scrollable, disclosed, or wrapping navigation and verify that focused links are visible—not merely focusable.",
